        "highlight_quote": "Our work begins with the observation that everyday wellbeing is shaped not only by occasional events, but by the experiences that life repeats most often.",
        "body": "<p>Much of everyday life unfolds through repeated encounters with the same environments, routines and sensory experiences. Over time, these repeated experiences become part of the background conditions that shape how daily life is felt.</p><p>The light we wake up to.</p><p>The pace of our mornings.</p><p>The sounds that fill our evenings.</p><p>The routines we repeat.</p><p>The spaces we spend time in.</p><p>Over time, repeated experiences contribute to whether daily life feels familiar, hurried, calm or restorative.</p><p>This observation guides everything we study, design and publish.</p><p>Rather than beginning with outcomes, we begin with the experiences that precede them—the moments of orientation, slowing, reflection and restoration that quietly shape the rhythm of everyday life.</p>"
