        "highlight_quote": "For us, rituals are not habits to be perfected. They are repeated sensory experiences that help create gentler transitions through everyday life.",
        "body": "<p>For most of human history, daily life contained natural transitions.</p><p>Morning light signalled the beginning of the day.</p><p>Shared meals created pauses between activities.</p><p>Evenings gradually softened into darkness and rest.</p><p>These moments helped create a rhythm between effort and recovery, attention and reflection, activity and rest.</p><p>Today many of those transitions have become less distinct.</p><p>Work continues beyond the workplace. Information remains constantly available. The same screens often accompany us from morning until sleep.</p><p>As the boundaries between different parts of the day become less defined, moments of recovery can become harder to access.</p>"
